<Docs title="Project Insights">
  <h1>Project Insights</h1>
  <p>
    MixRestore parses your Ableton Live Set files and extracts rich metadata,
    giving you a bird's-eye view of your project at any point in time.
  </p>

  <h2>Metadata</h2>
  <p>The project header displays key information at a glance:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>BPM</strong> — project tempo</li>
    <li><strong>Key</strong> — musical key and scale</li>
    <li><strong>Time Signature</strong> — e.g., 4/4, 3/4, 6/8</li>
    <li><strong>Ableton Version</strong> — which version of Live created the project</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Tracks</h2>
  <p>
    View a breakdown of your project's track types — audio, MIDI, return, and group tracks.
    Track counts update with each version so you can see how your project grew over time.
  </p>

  <h2>Arrangement</h2>
  <p>
    The arrangement visualization shows your project's locator-based sections as a
    horizontal bar chart. Each section is displayed proportionally based on its length
    in bars, giving you a visual overview of the song structure.
  </p>
  <p>Hover over any section to see its name and bar range.</p>

  <h2>Samples</h2>
  <p>
    MixRestore lists all audio samples used in the project. For each sample you can see:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>File name and relative path</li>
    <li>Whether it's a Splice sample (detected automatically)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Use the search filter to find specific samples, or copy the full sample list
    to your clipboard for reference.
  </p>
</Docs>
